---
import Docs from "../layouts/Docs.astro";
---

<Docs
  title="Documentation"
  description="Learn how to run and control Lowland Linux machines in browsers and Node.js."
  current=""
  headings={[]}
>
  <article class="docs-home">
    <p class="eyebrow">Lowland documentation</p>
    <h1>Linux is a JavaScript library.</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Boot a wasm32 Linux system in a browser or Node.js. Start with the guest API, or configure a
      machine and its virtio devices directly.
    </p>

    <section class="first-step">
      <div>
        <p class="step-number">01 · Tutorial</p>
        <h2>Boot your first machine</h2>
        <p>
          Start with one HTML file and no build tools. Add the required headers, boot Linux, and run
          <code>uname</code> from JavaScript.
        </p>
        <a class="strong-link" href="/getting-started/">Run Linux in your browser →</a>
      </div>
      <pre><code>{`const guest = guestAgent();
await bootMachine({
  cpus: 1,
  plugins: [guest],
});`}</code></pre>
    </section>

    <section class="paths" aria-labelledby="choose-a-path">
      <p class="step-number">02 · Choose a path</p>
      <h2 id="choose-a-path">Choose an API</h2>
      <div class="path-list">
        <article>
          <h3>Control a Linux guest</h3>
          <p>Run processes, read and write files, mount storage, and connect networks.</p>
          <ul>
            <li><a href="/reference/linux-guest/"><code>@lowland/guest</code> reference →</a></li>
            <li><a href="/attach-a-terminal/">Attach an interactive terminal →</a></li>
          </ul>
        </article>
        <article>
          <h3>Assemble a machine</h3>
          <p>Configure CPUs and memory, attach virtio devices, and control the boot lifecycle.</p>
          <ul>
            <li><a href="/reference/kernel/"><code>@lowland/kernel</code> reference →</a></li>
          </ul>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>
  </article>

</Docs>

<style>
  .eyebrow {
    margin-block: 0 0.75rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .docs-home h1 {
    max-width: 16ch;
    margin-block-start: 0;
    font-size: clamp(2.15rem, 5vw, 3.25rem);
    letter-spacing: -0.035em;
  }

  .lede {
    max-width: 60ch;
    font-size: 1.0625rem;
  }

  .first-step {
    margin-block-start: 2.75rem;
    padding-block: 1.5rem;
    border-block: 1px solid var(--hairline);
    display: grid;
    gap: 1.5rem;
  }

  .first-step h2,
  .paths h2 {
    margin-block-start: 0;
  }

  .step-number {
    margin-block-end: 0.5rem;
    color: var(--muted);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .first-step pre {
    margin: 0;
    align-self: center;
    padding: 1rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--hairline);
    background: var(--surface);
    font-size: 0.875rem;
  }

  .strong-link {
    color: var(--code-foreground);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .paths {
    margin-block-start: 2.75rem;
  }

  .path-list {
    margin-block-start: 1.25rem;
    border-block-start: 1px solid var(--hairline);
  }

  .path-list article {
    padding-block: 1.25rem;
    border-block-end: 1px solid var(--hairline);
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(10rem, 0.65fr) 1fr;
    column-gap: 1.5rem;

    > h3 {
      grid-row: 1 / span 2;
      margin: 0;
    }

    > p {
      margin-block-end: 0.65rem;
    }
  }

  .path-list ul {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 0.4rem 1rem;
    font-size: 0.875rem;
  }

  @media (max-width: 32rem) {
    .path-list article {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;

      > h3 {
        grid-row: auto;
        margin-block-end: 0.4rem;
      }
    }
  }

</style>
